+
+## Externally owned Sessions
+
+Host integrations can call `followReadOnly` after their own authorization. It retains the original journal and assistant frames without promoting a prepared Session to an Agent; the ordinary `follow` behavior stays unchanged. This method is not exposed as a Remote endpoint.
+
+Client integrations install `sessions.registerSessionDelegate(id, delegate)` before retaining a Session. The original Session, submission identities, event stream and reference counts remain the owners of Client state. Releasing or aborting the delegate invalidates that generation; later acquisitions require a new delegate, and stale references never fall back to ordinary RPC. Only page, follow, prompt and cancel have delegate adapters. Other mutations are unavailable for a delegated Session. Host authorization remains mandatory.
+
+Delegated history calls the Gateway stream factory with its original service receiver, preserving the Host connection and stream supervisor.
+
+Retained history can reopen through `sessions.restartHistory(id)` without replacing the Client Session, its visible window or pending submissions. A native owner disposal refreshes only its stored header and cached projections: durable Sessions remain in the catalog, missing Sessions are removed, and unknown metadata availability reports an error without certifying deletion.
